[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
open-media-drc — post-install checklist
=======================================

1. Configuration
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/omdrc.conf.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/omdrc.conf
   and edit (GEOMETRY, state dir).  The stack ships with FLAT (identity)
   filters — audio passes through unchanged until you install real room
   correction filters; see FILTERS_AND_DRC.md in the docs.

2. BruteFIR defaults (REQUIRED — brutefir fails to start without it):
   as the audio user:
     mkdir -p ~/.config/BruteFIR
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/open-media-drc/brutefir_defaults.conf.sample \
        ~/.config/BruteFIR/brutefir_defaults.conf
   The DAC is opened as /dev/dsp.dac, a symlink the omdrc_audio service
   maintains (sysrc omdrc_audio_enable=YES), so pcm unit numbers do not
   matter.  Adjust the OSS device paths inside only if you do not run it.

3. Kernel modules (in /etc/rc.conf or kld_list):
     kld_list="cuse"          # required by virtual_oss

4. MPD outputs: merge the example MPD config
   (%%PREFIX%%/share/examples/open-media-drc/musicpd.conf.in) into your mpd
   config — the OKTO-DAC / DRC-native / DRC-resamp output names are what
   drc.sh toggles with mpc.

   The installed %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.conf.d/musicpd/omdrc_audio fragment runs one
   bounded `service omdrc_audio reconcile` after a successful MPD start.  This
   repairs an output selection that was left pending when the physical DRC
   chain started before MPD; it does not make DRC depend on MPD readiness.
   If rc.conf.d/musicpd previously existed as a file, package installation
   preserves it unchanged as rc.conf.d/musicpd/00-local.conf before installing
   the separate hook.  rc.subr sources both files from the directory form.

5. Services, in /etc/rc.conf:
     musicpd_enable="YES"
     omdrc_audio_enable="YES"
     omdrc_audio_user="<audio user>"
   omdrc_audio owns the role links, boot/hotplug entry point and su -l user
   boundary.  Remove obsolete drc_usb_audio_*, brutefir_drc_* and
   omdrc_sndlink_* entries after migrating their local values.

   Also remove any hard-coded hw.snd.default_unit=N from /etc/sysctl.conf.
   PCM numbers follow USB attach order; omdrc_audio sets and verifies this
   value from the current DAC role on every boot/hotplug role transaction.

6. devd hotplug (follow the DAC and the capture card on plug/unplug):
     cp %%PREFIX%%/etc/devd/omdrc-audio.conf.sample \
        %%PREFIX%%/etc/devd/omdrc-audio.conf
     service devd restart

   The pcm attach/detach rules start a detached, idempotent
   `service omdrc_audio reconcile`.  They never match a keyboard or interpret
   an unrelated USB detach as a reason to stop audio.

7. Run `omdrc 192000` (or omdrc cdin / resamp / off / status) to drive the
   chain manually.  Power, rate and music/CD source persist together.  Pin
   OMDRC_STATE_DIR in omdrc.conf if service and interactive users differ.
EOM
}
]
